# What is a Vendor Prefix ? Its a First 3 Hex Values (Example0: "0F:0F:0F" Only Vendor Prefix, Example1: "0F:0F:0F:F0:F0:F0:" Full MAC)
#
# For Example Here is Lenovo Vendor MAC Prefix
# 10:C5:95
# 80:96:21
# A4:11:94
# A4:8C:DB
#
# By Default Lib_Gen_MAC.c Generates a (Random) MAC Address (On Every Boot, Not a ReBoot)
# But You Can Select On Firmware Setup Menu or PreConfigure Vendor Prefix 
# Avalible 3(4) Options,
# 0: Take / Generate Random MAC Vendor Prefix
# 1: Take A HW Based MAC Vendor Prefix, Based on CoreBoot MainBoard Vendor Name Configuration (MAINBOARD_VENDOR)
# 2: Manually Select a MAC Vendor Prefix
# 3: Manually Enter a MAC Vendor Prefix

